// Phase I benchmark: human-labelled explanations with rationales.
//
// One JSON object per line. Lines starting with // are comments and are
// skipped by the loader (see src/domain.py::_load_jsonl).
//
// READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING ANY NUMBER COMPUTED OVER THIS FILE
// -----------------------------------------------------------
// 1. It is CLASS-BALANCED, roughly 50/50 per criterion. Real explanation
//    defect rates are a few percent. A benchmark that matched production
//    would be ~95% PASS, and a judge that answered PASS to everything would
//    score 95% while catching nothing. Balance is what makes specificity
//    measurable at all. The cost is that NOTHING here estimates the live
//    defect rate, and any report that presents these as production quality
//    numbers is wrong.
//
// 2. It is DIFFICULTY-ENRICHED. Examples were written to sit near the
//    criterion boundary on purpose. Expect every judge, human or model, to
//    score lower here than on naturally sampled traffic. That is the point.
//
// 3. It is SMALL - roughly 20 labelled examples per criterion, against ~900
//    in the paper this is modelled on. A 25% test split is five or six
//    examples, so a single flipped verdict moves a metric by 15 points. The
//    evaluator prints Wilson confidence intervals for exactly this reason,
//    and they are wide. Treat differences under about 20 points here as
//    noise, grow the set with `run.py benchmark synthesise` and the weekly
//    Phase IV append, and re-read the intervals rather than the point
//    estimates.
//
// 4. Every FAIL carries a rationale AND a failure mode. This is not
//    documentation. The reasoning meta-judge compares the judge's stated
//    reason against the human's, so an example without a rationale is
//    invisible to reasoning agreement and RART degenerates to label-only
//    tuning. src/domain.py refuses to load a FAIL with no rationale.
//
// Cases marked BASELINE-MISS or BASELINE-FALSE-FAIL are where the rule-engine
// baseline (src/rules.py) disagrees with the human. They were written
// deliberately. They are the headroom RART optimises into, and the residue
// that no lexical rule can ever reach - which is the case for paying for a
// model judge, made measurable instead of asserted.

// =========================================================================
// CRITERION: grounded
// =========================================================================

{"id": "ex-g01", "record_id": "rec-001", "artefact": "The Quiet Harbour is a slow-burn mystery set in a fishing village, and it won three awards at Venice.", "labels": {"grounded": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"grounded": "The record lists no awards and never mentions Venice. Both are invented, and a reader has no way to check either."}, "failure_modes": {"grounded": "unsupported_claim"}, "source": "expert"}
