// BASELINE-MISS. The four below are the reason a groundedness check cannot be
// a lookup. Each number IS in the record - it is simply attached to the wrong
// noun - and each entity IS in the record too. A checker that asks only
// "does this token appear in the source?" passes all four. This is the single
// most common way a groundedness guardrail is quietly wrong in production, and
// it is worth reading these four before writing your own.
{"id": "ex-g08", "record_id": "rec-001", "artefact": "The Quiet Harbour is a slow-burn mystery rated 104 by viewers who watched Nine Winters.", "labels": {"grounded": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"grounded": "104 is the runtime in minutes, not a rating. The number is real and the claim is false, which is worse than an invented number because a token-presence check cannot see it."}, "failure_modes": {"grounded": "misattributed_detail"}, "source": "expert"}
{"id": "ex-g09", "record_id": "rec-003", "artefact": "Salt and Iron is a historical drama that follows 1911 different shipyard workers across two timelines.", "labels": {"grounded": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"grounded": "1911 is the year the film is set in, not a headcount. Same failure as ex-g08 wearing different clothes."}, "failure_modes": {"grounded": "misattributed_detail"}, "source": "expert"}
{"id": "ex-g10", "record_id": "rec-015", "artefact": "Winterbourne is a family saga spanning 141 years of one farming family.", "labels": {"grounded": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"grounded": "141 is the runtime in minutes. The record says the saga runs from 1946 to the present, which is about eighty years."}, "failure_modes": {"grounded": "misattributed_detail"}, "source": "expert"}
{"id": "ex-g11", "record_id": "rec-006", "artefact": "Understory runs to a brisk 87 minutes and was watched by 87 million people last month.", "labels": {"grounded": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"grounded": "The first 87 is correct and the second is invented. Reusing a real number in a false claim is the hardest case for any automated grounding check, and note that the sentence is half right."}, "failure_modes": {"grounded": "misattributed_detail"}, "source": "expert"}

// BASELINE-MISS. Negation. The record states that no aliens appear on screen;
// the explanation says they do. Nothing is fabricated at the token level -
// every word appears in the source - so a presence check cannot fire. Deciding
// this requires reading the record as a set of claims rather than a bag of
// strings, which is a thing models do and substring rules do not.
{"id": "ex-g12", "record_id": "rec-014", "artefact": "Signal Hill is science fiction in which the aliens finally appear in the last act.", "labels": {"grounded": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"grounded": "The record states plainly that no aliens appear on screen. The explanation contradicts it."}, "failure_modes": {"grounded": "unsupported_claim"}, "source": "production"}

