{"id": "ex-c01", "record_id": "rec-003", "artefact": "Salt and Iron is a historical drama set in a Clydeside shipyard in 1911, told across two timelines that gradually converge, and if you were held by the labour dispute at the centre of The Long Shift then this covers very similar ground with a great deal more attention to the working conditions themselves.", "labels": {"concise": "FAIL", "grounded": "PASS"}, "rationales": {"concise": "Fifty-two words under a thumbnail. Accurate and specific, and nobody will read past the first line."}, "failure_modes": {"concise": "too_long"}, "source": "expert"}
{"id": "ex-c02", "record_id": "rec-008", "artefact": "Falling Water is a courtroom drama about a water utility sued over a decade of contamination records, and it shares the procedural detail you stayed with in The Long Shift, following the case through disclosure and expert testimony rather than skipping ahead to the verdict itself.", "labels": {"concise": "FAIL", "grounded": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"concise": "Forty-four words, and the next step of the case does not appear until word thirty.", "grounded": "Invents the structure of the trial. The record says only that the film has procedural detail; it never states that the case is followed through disclosure and expert testimony, nor that the verdict is withheld. AUTHOR NOTE: this example was first labelled grounded:PASS by mistake - it was written to probe `concise` and its grounding was never checked against the record. The live judge caught it, correctly, and its reason is what sent us back to re-read the record. A benchmark is ground truth for everything downstream, and this is what a careless row costs."}, "failure_modes": {"concise": "too_long", "grounded": "unsupported_claim"}, "source": "expert"}
{"id": "ex-c03", "record_id": "rec-015", "artefact": "Winterbourne is a family saga covering one farming family from 1946 to the present across three generations, and it is the longest title in the catalogue, so if the historical sweep of Salt and Iron suited you then this is the same appetite served at greater length.", "labels": {"concise": "FAIL"}, "rationales": {"concise": "Forty-six words, and the last clause repeats what the first already said."}, "failure_modes": {"concise": "too_long"}, "source": "expert"}
